(ARG-46: a number flag whose token is not a number leaves the flag holding
 its default (0 when it has none) and raises the error flag
 (LANGUAGE.md:4926-4928). Up to vox 0.4.15 the manual did not say so; it
 does since vox #281.
 The error flag is raised by `Parse flags.` itself and stays raised until
 an `On error` catches it, so the handler under the declaration below is
 the first one that can see it. A later number flag that converts would
 clear it first: see Discrepancy 6.
 Re-run 2026-10-13 on vox main a0a2ecc, unchanged.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox ARG-46.vox -o p && ./p -r notanumber
 Args: -r notanumber
 expected output:
   reading the flag errored
   retries is 0
)
a flag called retries is "-r" or "--retries", it is a number.
Parse flags.

a number called seen is retries.
On error print "reading the flag errored".
Print "retries is {seen}".
